# Security

- Never commit API keys, tokens, private keys, passwords, service-account JSON, signing secrets, or production credentials.
- Do not print discovered secrets; report location only.
- Client-visible identifiers and server secrets must be separated.
- Auth/ownership checks must not rely only on client UI state.
- Production data must not be used as the default development test environment.
- High-impact actions such as delete, payment, permission escalation, and production deploy need explicit safeguards.
